682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[1,5,6,7,10,16,18,20]},{"id":"isaac_616","name":"Isaac","also":"","summary":"The only son of Abraham by Sarah. He was the longest lived of the three patriarchs (Gen. 21:1-3).","verses":123,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Sarah","v":[1,5,6,8,13]},{"id":"canaan_914","name":"Canaan","also":"Canaanites, Canaanite","summary":"The fourth son of Ham (Gen. 10:6). His descendants were under a curse in consequence of the transgression of his father (9:22-27). His eldest son, Zidon, was the father of the Sidonians and Phoenicians.","verses":84,"father":"Ham","mother":"","v":[1,6,8]},{"id":"laban_1803","name":"Laban","also":"","summary":"The son of Bethuel, who was the son of Nahor, Abraham’s brother. He lived at Haran in Mesopotamia. His sister Rebekah was Isaac’s wife (Gen. 24).","verses":46,"father":"Bethuel","mother":"","v":[2,5]},{"id":"bethuel_487","name":"Bethuel","also":"","summary":"The son of Nahor by Milcah; nephew of Abraham, and father of Rebekah (Gen. 22:22, 23; 24:15, 24, 47).","verses":9,"father":"Nahor","mother":"Milcah","v":[2,5]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[4,9,13]},{"id":"esau_1216","name":"Esau","also":"Edom, Edomite","summary":"Hairy, Rebekah’s first-born twin son (Gen. 25:25). The name of Edom, “red”, was also given to him from his conduct in connection with the red lentil “pottage” for which he sold his birthright (30, 31).","verses":151,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[5,6,8,9]},{"id":"rebekah_2401","name":"Rebekah","also":"","summary":"A noose, the daughter of Bethuel, and the wife of Isaac (Gen. 22:23; 24:67). The circumstances under which Abraham’s “steward” found her at the “city of Nahor,” in Padan-aram, are narrated in Gen. 24-27.","verses":29,"father":"Bethuel","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"ishmael_630","name":"Ishmael","also":"","summary":"Abraham’s eldest son, by Hagar the concubine (Gen. 16:15; 17:23). He was born at Mamre, when Abraham was eighty-six years of age, eleven years after his arrival in Canaan (16:3; 21:5).","verses":18,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Hagar","v":[9]},{"id":"bashemath_1887","name":"Bashemath","also":"Mahalath","summary":"The daughter of Ishmael, the last of Esau’s three wives (Gen. 36:3, 4, 13), from whose son Reuel four tribes of the Edomites sprung. She is also called Mahalath (Gen. 28:9).","verses":6,"father":"Ishmael","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"nebajoth_2164","name":"Nebajoth","also":"Nebaioth","summary":"Ishmael’s eldest son (Gen. 25:13), and the prince of an Israelitish tribe (16).","verses":5,"father":"Ishmael","mother":"","v":[9]}],"places":[{"id":"paddan-aram_916","name":"Paddan-aram","kind":"","lat":36.86386,"lon":39.0322,"summary":"The plain of Aram, or the plain of the highlands, (Gen. 25:20; 28:2, 5-7; 31:18, etc.), commonly regarded as the district of Mesopotamia lying around Haran.","verses":10,"v":[2,5,6,7]},{"id":"beersheba_170","name":"Beersheba","kind":"City","lat":31.245,"lon":34.84068,"summary":"Well of the oath, or well of seven, a well dug by Abraham, and so named because he and Abimelech here entered into a compact (Gen. 21:31). On re-opening it, Isaac gave it the same name (Gen. 26:31-33).","verses":32,"v":[10]},{"id":"haran_527","name":"Haran","kind":"City","lat":36.86,"lon":39.03139,"summary":"Heb. haran, i.e., “parched;” or probably from the Accadian charana, meaning “a road.” A celebrated city of Western Asia, now Harran, where Abram remained, after he left Ur of the Chaldees, till his father Terah died (Gen. 11:31, 32), when he continued his journey into the land of Canaan.","verses":10,"v":[10]},{"id":"bethel_202","name":"Bethel","kind":"","lat":31.93054,"lon":35.22103,"summary":"A place in Central Palestine, about 10 miles north of Jerusalem, at the head of the pass of Michmash and Ai. It was originally the royal Canaanite city of Luz (Gen. 28:19).","verses":62,"v":[19]},{"id":"luz_737","name":"Luz","kind":"City","lat":31.93054,"lon":35.22103,"summary":"The ancient name of a royal Canaanitish city near the site of Bethel (Gen. 28:19; 35:6), on the border of Benjamin (Josh. 18:13).","verses":6,"v":[19]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3327,3327,7121,7121,3290,1288,1288,853,3808,3808,3947,802,802,3667,3667,3667,1323,6680,6680],[1980,6965,6965,758,758,1004,1004,1004,517,517,517,1,1328,3947,3947,802,802,1323,1323,1323,1323,3837,3837,517,517,251],[410,410,7706,1288,853,6509,6509,6509,6509,7235,7235,7235,1961,1961,1961,1961,1961,6951,6951,5971,5971],[5414,5414,5414,5414,1293,1293,85,85,0,0,2233,2233,2233,3423,3423,3423,3423,3423,776,776,4033,4033,4033,4033,4033,4033,834,834,430,5414,85,85],[3327,3327,7971,3290,758,758,413,3837,1121,1328,1328,761,761,251,251,7259,7259,517,517,517,517,3290,3290,6215,6215],[6215,6215,7200,3588,3327,1288,1288,3290,7971,7971,853,758,758,3947,3947,802,802,8033,6680,5921,3808,3808,3947,3667,3667,1323],[3290,3290,3290,8085,8085,1,1,517,517,1980,1980,758,758],[6215,7200,3588,1,1,3327,7451,7451,3667,3667,1323],[6215,1980,413,3458,3947,3947,4258,269,269,5032,5032,1323,1323,85,85,1121,3458,5921,5921,5921,802,802,0,0,0],[3290,3290,3318,884,1980,1980,1980,1980,2771],[6293,6293,4725,4725,4725,3885,3885,3885,3885,8033,3588,8121,8121,935,935,3947,3947,68,68,68,68,4725,4725,4725,7760,7760,4763,4763,4763,4763,7901,7901,7901,4725,4725],[2492,2492,2492,2492,2492,2009,5551,5551,5324,5324,776,776,776,72